&lt;p&gt;As a Senior Product Engineer on the Tooling team, you&#39;ll work across backend, web, and mobile to build the customer-facing platform tooling that shapes how millions of users experience Gemini - onboarding, compliance, customer support, and the ad hoc projects that keep the customer journey smooth from first touch onward. This is a broad, high-ownership role for an engineer who is comfortable moving up and down the stack, picking up whatever a problem requires, and shipping products end to end.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;You&#39;ll join a team that treats AI-assisted development and automation as first-class tools. We run an agentic SDLC pipeline where specialized agents plan, implement and review work through our harness with human guidance. We expect our engineers to wield these tools fluently - offloading toil to automation while holding the decision gates that matter. If you get excited about solving customer-facing problems, working across domains rather than within a single specialty, and pushing the frontier of how software gets built, we&#39;d love to hear from you.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;&lt;em&gt;This role is required to be in person twice a week at our New York City, NY office.&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Responsibilities:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Design, develop, and deploy customer-facing features spanning backend services, web, and mobile - owning solutions end to end rather than within a single layer.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Build the platform tooling behind onboarding, compliance (KYC/identity), and customer support workflows that serve millions of users.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Leverage AI coding tools and our agentic development pipeline to move faster, and help improve the automation itself.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Own the DevOps lifecycle for the products you build: building, validating, monitoring, and maintaining them over their lifetime.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Provide technical input to planning, design, and requirements for new products and features, making well-reasoned tradeoffs between speed and quality.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Conduct meaningful code reviews for correctness, style, and information security.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Mentor engineers, share best practices, and contribute to the technical direction and engineering culture of the team.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Take on ambiguous, cross-cutting problems and drive them to resolution independently.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Minimum Qualifications:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;4+ years of software engineering experience building and maintaining production systems at scale.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Demonstrated ability to work across multiple layers of the stack: backend services plus web and/or mobile - and a willingness to work wherever a problem requires.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Proficiency in a typed language (e.g., TypeScript, Scala, Java, Go) and comfort with JavaScript/TypeScript for web and mobile surfaces.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience building consumer-facing applications, with a strong understanding of UX/UI concepts and product sensibility.&lt;/li&gt;
